# Security and child privacy — nrscholar-frontend

The users are children. Protect their data and keep parent controls intact. For a full review, use the `security-review` skill.

## Child safety

- The **parental gate** (`ParentalGateScreen`) and parent-only routes must stay enforced. Never add a route or deep link that reaches parent screens (settings, subscription, reports) without passing the gate. The backend must also enforce parent-only APIs.
- **Screen-time limits** (the tracker in `App.tsx`) must not be bypassable through new routes or WebView paths.
- Collect only what the feature needs. Don't add new personal fields, location, contacts, or open-ended chat/sharing between children without explicit product approval.
- No third-party analytics, ads or tracking SDKs without approval. Never send children's names, photos, scans or answers to third parties.
- Child-facing content and AI chat replies shown to children are displayed as text (no raw HTML).

## Tokens and sessions

- Tokens live in `localStorage` on the web (existing) and `expo-secure-store` on the device. Don't store tokens anywhere new. Always clear via `clearAuthSession()` / `removeToken()`.
- **Don't put tokens or personal data in URLs.** The current `?token=` handoff is a known risk (see the `mobile-and-webview` rule). Don't extend it.
- Escape anything injected into WebView JavaScript (`JSON.stringify`).

## Web

- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with server or user content.
- External links: `target="_blank"` + `rel="noopener noreferrer"`. Validate redirect targets.
- No secrets in `VITE_*` variables or source (they're public). Never read `.env*`.
- Uploads/scans (`ScanAndLearn`): restrict type and size, and send them only to our backend.

## Mobile

- Request permissions (camera, notifications) only when the feature needs them, with a clear reason string in `app.json`.
- The WebView `onMessage` handler validates message types. Restrict navigation to our domains.

## Payments / subscriptions

Prices and entitlement come from the backend. The client never decides that a subscription is active.
